{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1272268-limetown","id":1272268,"title":"Limetown","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-01T17:44:02-08:00","id":1272268,"title":"Limetown","content":"Are you familiar with <i>Limetown</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> For those who do not know,&quot;<i>Limetown</i> is a podcast fiction series created by Two-Up Productions that debuted on July 29, 2015, and became the number one US podcast on iTunes less than two months later. The show has drawn comparisons to the popular podcast <i>Serial</i> and the 1990s television show <i>The X-Files</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Further, &quot;Limetown is a fictional story told as a series of investigative reports by Lia Haddock (played by Annie-Sage Whitehurst), a journalist for American Public Radio (APR), detailing the disappearance of over 300 people at a neuroscience research facility in Tennessee.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I am posting this here because the podcast has a very <i>World of Darkness</i> vibe to it, without mentioning vampires, magic, and the like. The world is a dreadful place, full of unpleasant people, and there is a sinister cabal pursuing an malevolent conspiracy. <br /> <br /> <br /> If you start - and I am recommending it - please start at the beginning of Season One. If you jump in now, you will find it hard to follow. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}